Since our Rocky Linux 8.7 system requires root privileges for standard Nix installation and nix-portable seems not compatible with the installation instructions detailed in the documentation of nain4 project, we'll use Apptainer containers to provide you with a fully functional Nix environment. For more information about using Apptainer on our cluster, please refer to our documentation at: https://scc.dipc.org/docs/software/containers/apptainer/

==========================
INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS
==========================
--------------------------------------
STEP 1: Initial Setup (One-time only)
--------------------------------------
0. Log in to Hyperion(Atlas is not suitable for nix):
ssh hyperion
srun -N1 -n1 --mem=16g --time=24:00:00 --pty /bin/bash
(require a node to run with a 16 GB memory and a time of 24 hours)

1. cd to lscratch and load the Apptainer module:
cd /lscratch/$USER
module load Apptainer

2. Pull the Nix container image:
apptainer pull docker://nixos/nix:2.32.1

3. Create a writable sandbox from the image:
apptainer build --sandbox nix-sandbox/ nix_2.32.1.sif

4. Create necessary mount points in the sandbox:
mkdir -p nix-sandbox/scratch && mkdir -p nix-sandbox/lscratch && mkdir -p nix-sandbox/dipc && mkdir -p nix-sandbox/data && mkdir -p nix-sandbox/home

----------------------------------
STEP 2: Create Your nain4 Project
----------------------------------
Bootstrap a new nain4 project (replace "my-project" with your desired project name):
apptainer exec --writable -B /lscratch:/lscratch nix-sandbox/ nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' run github:jacg/nain4#bootstrap-client-project /lscratch/$USER/neutron_bg neutron_bg "Neutron background simulation"
(Note: This initial setup may take 30-60 minutes as it downloads all necessary dependencies.)

-------------------------------
STEP 3: Work with Your Project
-------------------------------
1. Navigate to your project:
cd /lscratch/$USER/neutron_bg

2. Enter the development environment:
apptainer exec --writable -B /lscratch:/lscratch /lscratch/$USER/nix-sandbox/ nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' develop
(You're now in a shell with all nain4 dependencies (Geant4, ROOT, etc.) available.)

3. Move the folders and files to /scratch/ (in /lscratch/$USER):
chmod -R 777 nix-sandbox/ && mv nix-sandbox/ /scratch/$USER/ && mv nix_2.32.1.sif /scratch/$USER/ && mv neutron_bg/ /scratch/$USER/

4. Usage of the project(in the container):
just install
just run -n 1000
just run-no-install -n 1000

Note 1: One needs to customize the macros, the source cc file, the justfile.
Note 2: /scratch/ directory is for submittng jobs to the cluster.

----------------------------------------
STEP 4: Convenience Setup (Recommended)
----------------------------------------
To simplify daily use, add these lines to your ~/.bashrc file:

# Nix/nain4 aliases
alias nix-shell='apptainer exec --writable -B /scratch:/scratch /scratch/$USER/nix-sandbox/ nix --extra-experimental-features "nix-command flakes"'
alias nain4-dev='cd /scratch/$USER/my-neutrino-project && apptainer exec --writable -B /scratch:/scratch /scratch/$USER/nix-sandbox/ nix --extra-experimental-features "nix-command flakes" develop'

# Then reload your bashrc:
source ~/.bashrc

--------------------------------
STEP 5: Using nain4 in HPC Jobs
--------------------------------
Simplified example SLURM job script (batch_script.slurm):

#!/bin/bash
#SBATCH --job-name=xxx
#SBATCH --partition=general
#SBATCH --qos=regular
#SBATCH --nodes=1
#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=1
#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=1
#SBATCH --array=0-99
#SBATCH --mem=16G
#SBATCH --time=24:00:00
#SBATCH --output=xxx_%j.out
#SBATCH --error=xxx_%j.err
#SBATCH --mail-user=xxx@dipc.org
#SBATCH --mail-type=ALL

module load Apptainer
cd /scratch/$USER/my-project
apptainer exec --writable -B /scratch:/scratch /scratch/$USER/nix-sandbox/ nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' develop --command bash -c "just run-no-install -n 100000000 ${SLURM_JOB_ID}"

------------------
STEP 6: Send jobs
------------------
From any location in /scratch/$USER, execute this:
sbatch batch_script.slurm

================
IMPORTANT NOTES
================
1. Warnings: You can safely ignore warnings about "passwd file doesn't exist"
  and "group file doesn't exist". These don't affect functionality.
2. Documentation: For more details about Apptainer on our cluster, visit:
  https://scc.dipc.org/docs/software/containers/apptainer/
